\nonumber\]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-134630"><strong>Region 3 Continued: </strong>After <em>addition of, say 99.90 mL of NaOH. </em>The solution contains further reduced strong acid and the total volume is 199.90 mL.</p>

<p class="lt-chem-134630">\[<br />
\left[ \mathrm { Na } ^ { + } \right] = \frac { ( 0.0999 \mathrm { L } ) ( 0.100 \mathrm { mol/L } ) } { ( 0.199 \mathrm { L } ) } = 0.04998 \mathrm { mol } / \mathrm { L }<br />
\nonumber\]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-134630">\[<br />
[ \mathrm { Cl ^-} ] = \frac { ( 0.100 \mathrm { L } ) ( 0.100 \mathrm { mol } / \mathrm { L } ) } { ( 0.1999 \mathrm { L } ) } = 0.05003 \mathrm { mol } / \mathrm { L }<br />
\nonumber\]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-134630">\[<br />
{ \left[ \mathrm { H } ^ { + } \right] = \mathbf { C } _ { \mathrm { a } } = } { \frac { ( 0.100 \mathrm { L } ) ( 0.100 \mathrm { mol } / \mathrm { L } ) - ( 0.0999 \mathrm { L } ) ( 0.100 \mathrm { mol } / \mathrm { L } ) } { ( 0.1999 \mathrm { L } ) } = 5.00 \times 10 ^ { - 5 } \mathrm { mol } / \mathrm { L } }<br />
\nonumber\]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-134630">\[<br />
