{ [ \mathrm { OH^- } ] = \mathrm { C } _ { \mathrm { b } } = } { \frac { ( 0.1001 \mathrm { L } ) ( 0.100 \mathrm { mol } / \mathrm { L } ) - ( 0.100 \mathrm { L } ) ( 0.100 \mathrm { mol } / \mathrm { L } ) } { ( 0.2001 \mathrm { L } ) } = 4.9975 \times 10 ^ { 5 } \mathrm { mol } / \mathrm { L } }<br />
\nonumber\]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-134630">\[<br />
\left[ \mathrm { H } ^ { + } \right] = \frac { 1.00 \times 10 ^ { - 14 } } { \left( 4.9975 \times 10 ^ { - 5 } \right) } = 2.001 \times 10 ^ { - 10 } \mathrm { mol } / \mathrm { L }<br />
\nonumber\]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-134630"><strong>Region 4 Continued: </strong>After <em>addition of 110.00 mL of NaOH. </em>The solution contains more strong base and the total volume is 210.00 mL.</p>

